[{"type": "note", "text": "Ninth extinction, year 17,421, and the proven genome half-worked. Seeding five real animals out of the year 14,500 archive with all 167 of their brain weights cut the irruption from 28-fold to 4-fold: 125 founders became 486 rather than 8,349. That is the first time any change has moved that number, and it confirms the brain was a real part of the problem. It was not enough. 486 animals still took the standing crop from 9,092 to 185 in four years, and then the population died out while the flora recovered past it -- 59 animals at a crop of 1,287, when the same world held 377 animals at a crop of 1,666 for centuries. That is the anomaly, and the endgame numbers explain it. The breeding bar rose as the population fell: 23.5, then 31.7, 33.8, 30.4. Percentage of animals above their own bar: 20, then 7, 3, 0. The famine was selecting repro_threshold upward. An animal that breeds during a crash gives its energy away and dies; an animal that hoards survives. So the survivors of a crash are precisely the individuals least able to rebuild the population, and by the time the grass comes back the only ones left are constitutionally incapable of using it. Every crash in this world's history has been running that ratchet, and it is why the deaths are absorbing: it is not that the survivors are too few, it is that the survivors are the wrong ones. The way out is to never have the crash. The irruption is driven by arrival wealth: founder_energy_mult is 3.5, so founders land with about 77 energy against a bar near 21 and every one of them breeds immediately, and so do their children, before anything has learned what the pasture can bear. Setting it to 1.0 lands them at 22 -- a hair above their own threshold -- so the founding population grows at the rate the grass allows instead of at the rate their subsidy allows. That value was raised to 3.5 for a real reason, seeded predator waves starving before their first kill, but this is a herbivore founding into a standing crop of five thousand and the reason does not apply. Seven proven animals this time rather than five, fifty each, 350 founders -- the size of the population this world actually held at year 14,500 -- spread across seven sites. No other laws touched."}, {"type": "tune", "path": "fauna.founder_energy_mult", "value": 1.0}, {"type": "seed_organism", "kingdom": "fauna", "count": 50, "x": 16, "y": 208, "radius": 22, "genome": {"size": 0.1447, "speed": 0.93, "metabolism_eff": 1.0, "sense_range": 0.2052, "camouflage": 0.787, "armor": 0.8229, "fangs": 1.0, "toxin_tolerance": 0.8882, "heat_tol": 0.886, "cold_tol": 0.9949, "lifespan": 0.9131, "repro_threshold": 0.2302, "repro_invest": 0.12, "sexual": 0.1287, "social": 0.2942, "scent_deposit": 0.7808, "swim": 0.1566, "diet": 0.0, "w000": -0.3612, "w001": 0.9259, "w002": 0.4089, "w003": 1.1242, "w004": -0.0836, "w005": 0.7401, "w006": -0.5085, "w007": 0.1183, "w008": -0.769, "w009": 0.4289, "w010": -0.3384, "w011": -0.8761, "w012": 1.1325, "w013": 0.1835, "w014": -0.0819, "w015": -0.5103, "w016": 0.415, "w017": 0.9991, "w018": 1.1759, "w019": -0.274, "w020": 0.0921, "w021": 0.7469, "w022": -0.2343, "w023": 0.1826, "w024": 0.2874, "w025": -1.188, "w026": 0.5883, "w027": -0.7438, "w028": 1.0807, "w029": 0.7409, "w030": -0.0112, "w031": 0.5632, "w032": -0.2143, "w033": -0.3559, "w034": -0.1466, "w035": 1.4739, "w036": -0.8155, "w037": 0.3608, "w038": 0.1747, "w039": -0.8599, "w040": -0.0297, "w041": 0.1539, "w042": -0.0497, "w043": 0.4045, "w044": 0.5513, "w045": 1.7308, "w046": 0.915, "w047": -0.5964, "w048": -0.5446, "w049": 1.6212, "w050": -1.4787, "w051": -0.1244, "w052": 0.9349, "w053": -0.3635, "w054": 1.313, "w055": 0.3942, "w056": 0.3998, "w057": 0.8743, "w058": -0.3355, "w059": -0.1052, "w060": 0.5066, "w061": 1.0716, "w062": -0.4411, "w063": -0.8946, "w064": -0.1868, "w065": -0.6248, "w066": -0.0539, "w067": -0.4144, "w068": 1.3633, "w069": -0.6951, "w070": 2.4368, "w071": -1.1173, "w072": -0.8167, "w073": 1.0